  - Not in his beak.

247
00:09:46,208 --> 00:09:47,750
 I worked on it myself.

248
00:09:49,833 --> 00:09:51,583
- That wouldn't make any
difference if he moved

249
00:09:51,583 --> 00:09:53,958
 the speed shift or something.
 - [Crow] Aw, shut up, pee wee.

250
00:09:53,958 --> 00:09:54,750
 - [Joel] Yeah.

251
00:09:59,167 --> 00:10:01,042
 - What kept you so long, Lisa?

252
00:10:01,042 --> 00:10:04,292
 - Mr. Willis smoked two cigars
 at the table after dinner.

253
00:10:04,292 --> 00:10:06,042
 And I couldn't get up.

254
00:10:06,042 --> 00:10:09,542
 - [Tom] Whoa, whoa, whoa,
 honey, speak English, will ya?

255
00:10:09,542 --> 00:10:11,250
  - Pat did not come
  home for this.

256
00:10:11,250 --> 00:10:13,167
That's why his father was upset.

257
00:10:14,417 --> 00:10:16,250
 - [Crow] Here, drink this,
 it'll make you feel American.

258
00:10:16,250 --> 00:10:18,083
  - There's old man Harris.

259
00:10:18,083 --> 00:10:23,083
 (Tom, Joel, and Crow humming
 "The Munsters" theme song)

260
00:10:24,292 --> 00:10:26,042
  - That fella has
  a jewel of a car.

261
00:10:26,042 --> 00:10:27,125
- [Tom] Let me think about that.

262
00:10:27,125 --> 00:10:28,875
 Okay.

263
00:10:28,875 --> 00:10:31,333
  (laughing)

264
00:10:31,333 --> 00:10:33,208
 - [Crow] Hoiman,
 wait here in the car!

265
00:10:35,208 --> 00:10:38,167
 - [Tom] Looks like this is
 where old jalopies go to die.

266
00:10:38,167 --> 00:10:40,667
 - [Joel] It's TV's
 lovable Stringbean!

267
00:10:40,667 --> 00:10:42,875
  (cheering)

268
00:10:42,875 --> 00:10:44,000
 - You wanna sell that deuce?

269
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:44,958
- [Crow] My little deuce coupe?

270
00:10:44,958 --> 00:10:47,000
  You don't know what I got!

271
00:10:47,000 --> 00:10:50,167
- Why you fellers always
askin' me to buy my car?

272
00:10:50,167 --> 00:10:52,792
 - That 32 is the ideal
 stock to convert to a bomb.

273
00:10:52,792 --> 00:10:54,000
- [Joel] Why do you guys
always throw me down

274
00:10:54,000 --> 00:10:56,000
 and steal my wallet?

275
00:10:56,000 --> 00:10:57,083
- It's just like
gettin' married.

276
00:10:57,083 --> 00:10:59,208
  Or going to New York City.

277
00:10:59,208 --> 00:11:01,667
 - [Joel, Tom, Crow]
 New York City!

278
00:11:01,667 --> 00:11:03,417
 - [Joel] Get the rope.

279
00:11:03,417 --> 00:11:04,625
  (laughing)

280
00:11:04,625 --> 00:11:06,208
 Available for parties
 and barmitzvers.

281
00:11:06,208 --> 00:11:07,583
 - I could get you a
 good price on that.

282
00:11:09,125 --> 00:11:10,500
 - [Voiceover] Again
 with the finger.

283
00:11:10,500 --> 00:11:13,792
 - It's $695 for that
 car 26 years ago.

284
00:11:13,792 --> 00:11:16,708
 10 years ago,
 wasn't worth a dime.

285
00:11:16,708 --> 00:11:19,000
 Last month, I turned
 down 100 for it.

286
00:11:20,000 --> 00:11:23,625
When it gets back up to
695 again, I'll sell it.

287
00:11:23,625 --> 00:11:25,958
  (laughing)

288
00:11:27,250 --> 00:11:28,542
  Hey Spook,

289
00:11:28,542 --> 00:11:31,625
 give me a snort of
 that there sody pop.

290
00:11:31,625 --> 00:11:32,917
  (laughing)

291
00:11:32,917 --> 00:11:34,125
- [Crow] 'Scuse me, that
one just slipped out.

292
00:11:34,125 --> 00:11:35,417
 - Hey gang, you know
 this will be Lisa's

293
00:11:35,417 --> 00:11:36,708
  first trip to a drive-in?

294
00:11:36,708 --> 00:11:38,500
- Aw, we have drive-ins
in France, too.

295
00:11:38,500 --> 00:11:41,083
- [Voiceover] Wee, they
play Jerry Lewis movies.

296
00:11:41,083 --> 00:11:43,167
- I went with my brother
on his motor scooter.

297
00:11:43,167 --> 00:11:44,208
  (laughing)

298
00:11:44,208 --> 00:11:46,250
- [Joel] Looks like
he's filling the bottle.

299
00:11:46,250 --> 00:11:47,583
  (groaning)

300
00:11:47,583 --> 00:11:49,542
 - [Crow] Who put sody
 pop in my sody pop?

301
00:11:53,583 --> 00:11:55,667
 - [Tom] Hey, let's go
 do some crimes, man.

302
00:11:57,292 --> 00:12:00,125
- If the road's clear, I'll
drag you to Bartinell's corner.

303
00:12:00,125 --> 00:12:02,125
 - [Crow] Drag me, I'll
 get the tow chain.

304
00:12:03,375 --> 00:12:04,542
 - [Voiceover] You still
 runnin' on that old rubber?

305
00:12:04,542 --> 00:12:05,917
- [Joel] Old rubber, no, no, no!

306
00:12:05,917 --> 00:12:08,333
 - Hey Spook, when
 Pat and Liz get here,

307
00:12:08,333 --> 00:12:10,083
 will you tell them we
 went to the drive-in

308
00:12:10,083 --> 00:12:12,000
  and for them to catch up?

309
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:12,833
  Thank you.

310
00:12:12,833 --> 00:12:14,583
- We sure will.

311
00:12:14,583 --> 00:12:16,708
 - And I'll give you 150 bucks.

312
00:12:16,708 --> 00:12:18,000
- [Crow] To take acting lessons.

313
00:12:18,000 --> 00:12:20,667
  - You're talking
  like my butchers.

314
00:12:20,667 --> 00:12:22,583
 - [Joel] Okay, 'nuff
 said, old timer.

315
00:12:22,583 --> 00:12:24,542
 - What are you
 playin' with, kids?

316
00:12:24,542 --> 00:12:27,458
  (laughing)

317
00:12:27,458 --> 00:12:28,958
- [Tom] Oh, it's red man juice.

318
00:12:28,958 --> 00:12:30,333
  (groaning)

319
00:12:30,333 --> 00:12:32,042
 - [Joel] That guy cracks me
 up. I don't know, do you?

320
00:12:33,125 --> 00:12:34,375
- [Tom] One-Adam
12, one-Adam 12,

321
00:12:34,375 --> 00:12:36,125
what are you doing in Wisconsin?

322
00:12:37,958 --> 00:12:40,417
- [Crow] Selznick International
Pictures presents.

323
00:12:41,917 --> 00:12:44,542
 - [Tom] I'm Sebastian Cabot,
 and this is Ghost Story.

324
00:12:52,833 --> 00:12:55,083
- [Tom] Well gel there program.

325
00:12:55,083 --> 00:12:56,417
  - Pat didn't come
  home last night.

326
00:12:56,417 --> 00:12:57,958
 - He didn't?

327
00:12:57,958 --> 00:12:59,875
- No, evidently he was
out with Liz Humphries.

328
00:12:59,875 --> 00:13:01,625
 She didn't come home either.

329
00:13:01,625 --> 00:13:03,125
- [Joel] When you due, Sheriff?

330
00:13:03,125 --> 00:13:05,000
 - I want you to find out why.

331
00:13:05,000 --> 00:13:07,500
And don't leave a stone
unturned in doing so.

332
00:13:07,500 --> 00:13:09,208
Do I make myself clear?

333
00:13:09,208 --> 00:13:11,000
 - I understand Mr. Wheeler.

334
00:13:11,000 --> 00:13:12,667
  - [Crow] That's a
  well fitting suit.

335
00:13:12,667 --> 00:13:14,000
 - Wrecks reported last night.

336
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:18,417
  Your son, Pat,
  about 19 isn't he?

337
00:13:18,417 --> 00:13:19,333
- That's right.

338
00:13:19,333 --> 00:13:20,625
  - [Joel] As teens go, yes.

339
00:13:20,625 --> 00:13:22,167
- A year older than I
was when I got married.

340
00:13:22,167 --> 00:13:23,667
- You think they eloped?

341
00:13:23,667 --> 00:13:25,917
 - [Tom] No, they can't
 elope, they're fruit, get it?

342
00:13:25,917 --> 00:13:28,250
 - I didn't say that.

343
00:13:28,250 --> 00:13:30,000
 But if they were out
 together all night,

344
00:13:30,000 --> 00:13:31,375
  you better hope they have.

345
00:13:31,375 --> 00:13:33,083
 - This is a missing
 person's report

346
00:13:33,083 --> 00:13:34,667
 and I want to know what
 you're going to do about it.

347
00:13:34,667 --> 00:13:39,083
 - Well, I'll send in an APB
 on both of them and the car.

348
00:13:39,083 --> 00:13:40,208
I don't think it'll do much good

349
00:13:40,208 --> 00:13:41,208
if they went off to get married,

350
00:13:41,208 --> 00:13:43,208
 they'd already be
 across the state line.

351
00:13:43,208 --> 00:13:45,000
  - Why, if he got married,
  I'll ring his neck.

352
00:13:45,000 --> 00:13:46,667
- [Crow] That Jerry
Lee, he's done it again!

353
00:13:46,667 --> 00:13:49,083
 - If you ask me, it's
 that Chase Winston.

354
00:13:49,083 --> 00:13:50,083
 He's older than the others.

355
00:13:50,083 --> 00:13:52,042
 Sets them all wrong.

356
00:13:52,042 --> 00:13:54,583
 Why he's got more influence
 on Pat than I have.

357
00:13:54,583 --> 00:13:56,042
 - [Tom] Hooker's a good cop.

358
00:13:56,042 --> 00:13:57,833
  - Chase Winston does more
  about keeping them in line

359
00:13:57,833 --> 00:13:59,875
 then getting them in
 trouble and I know.

360
00:13:59,875 --> 00:14:01,458
  He's supported his
  mother and sister

361
00:14:01,458 --> 00:14:04,333
ever since his dad on
one of your drill rings.

362
00:14:04,333 --> 00:14:06,625
 Your son could take a page
 outta his book Mr. Wheeler.

363
00:14:06,625 --> 00:14:08,208
  - [Joel] Ooh, what a burn.

364
00:14:08,208 --> 00:14:10,667
- When I get through with my
son, he won't have a book left.

365
00:14:10,667 --> 00:14:12,875
 Now you locate him,
 or I'll have your job.

366
00:14:12,875 --> 00:14:14,500
 - If you want to be
 the only peace officer

367
00:14:14,500 --> 00:14:17,583
in 10,000 square miles
and 1,000 miles of road,

368
00:14:17,583 --> 00:14:18,833
 you're welcome to it.

369
00:14:18,833 --> 00:14:21,125
- [Crow] This is my
world and welcome to it.

370
00:14:21,125 --> 00:14:23,708
  - I'll do everything I can
  to locate both of them.

371
00:14:23,708 --> 00:14:26,125
  - [Voiceover] Go on home,
  they're waiting for you.

372
00:14:27,417 --> 00:14:28,333
  (barking)

373
00:14:28,333 --> 00:14:31,917
  (upbeat electronic music)

374
00:14:35,250 --> 00:14:36,042
  - [Voiceover] Hi, Sheriff.

375
00:14:36,042 --> 00:14:37,083
 - [Crow] Wish I were.

376
00:14:37,083 --> 00:14:39,125
  (laughing)

377
00:14:42,417 --> 00:14:45,000
  - [Tom] What is this, The
  Misfits all of the sudden?

378
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:47,250
  - Yeah, new to me.

379
00:14:47,250 --> 00:14:48,458
 That's the biker I am.

380
00:14:48,458 --> 00:14:52,125
I'd be chasin' bicycles
a couple of days.

381
00:14:52,125 --> 00:14:53,000
 - Aw, come on Sheriff.

382
00:14:53,000 --> 00:14:54,667
Outside of Pat Wheeler,

383
00:14:54,667 --> 00:14:56,750
  we haven't had a ticket in
  our gang in eight months.

384
00:14:56,750 --> 00:14:58,042
 - I was just kidding.

385
00:14:58,042 --> 00:15:01,042
- [Joel] How much for
the macaroni and cheese.

386
00:15:01,042 --> 00:15:02,042
 - What's the mileage on it?

387
00:15:02,042 --> 00:15:04,500
 - Oh, about 35,000.

388
00:15:04,500 --> 00:15:06,125
 Tell him you bought
 it from the state.

389
00:15:06,125 --> 00:15:10,167
 Those lucky stiffs on highway
 get a new car every year.

390
00:15:10,167 --> 00:15:11,375
 - Let me have it
 for a couple of days

391
00:15:11,375 --> 00:15:12,583
 and I'll tune it up for you.

392
00:15:12,583 --> 00:15:14,042
  (laughing)

393
00:15:14,042 --> 00:15:16,708
- You'd joke it off so
I could never catch it.

394
00:15:16,708 --> 00:15:19,958
  - You couldn't catch that
  deuce of mine right now.

395
00:15:19,958 --> 00:15:21,625
Now let me have that patrol car.

396
00:15:21,625 --> 00:15:24,208
 I'll turn it into a slingshot
 that'll catch anything.

397
00:15:24,208 --> 00:15:26,375
 - [Tom] A Joe Namath
 netted slingshot.

398
00:15:29,167 --> 00:15:31,458
  (grunting)

399
00:15:33,375 --> 00:15:35,917
- [Joel] What do
you dream about?

400
00:15:35,917 --> 00:15:38,125
  - Just between us, Liz
  Humphries and Pat Wheeler

401
00:15:38,125 --> 00:15:39,750
 didn't get home last night.

402
00:15:41,208 --> 00:15:42,417
- They were supposed to
meet us at the drive-in

403
00:15:42,417 --> 00:15:44,125
but they didn't show up.

404
00:15:44,125 --> 00:15:45,750
  I wondered what happened.

405
00:15:45,750 --> 00:15:47,000
 - [Tom] Hec Ramsey!

406
00:15:47,000 --> 00:15:49,792
  - Are they in any
  kind of trouble?

407
00:15:49,792 --> 00:15:51,708
 - What do you mean?

408
00:15:51,708 --> 00:15:52,625
 - You know.

409
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:57,417
 - [Joel] You know, like Warren
 Beatty and Annette Bening?

410
00:15:57,417 --> 00:15:59,000
- No, I don't think so.

411
00:16:00,542 --> 00:16:04,083
 - Chase, level with me.
 - [Crow] You think I'm pretty?

412
00:16:04,083 --> 00:16:05,958
  - I'm almost positive they
  weren't in any trouble.

413
00:16:05,958 --> 00:16:07,083
  I'd know.

414
00:16:07,083 --> 00:16:08,708
 - [Joel] Mechanics intuition.

415
00:16:08,708 --> 00:16:10,667
  - You think they might've
  run off to get married?

416
00:16:12,083 --> 00:16:14,750
 - They've been going
 steady for over a year now.

417
00:16:14,750 --> 00:16:16,833
 I know they talked about it.

418
00:16:16,833 --> 00:16:18,417
 - [Tom] Well sir,
 person's got urges.

419
00:16:18,417 --> 00:16:20,292
 - Not for right now.

420
00:16:20,292 --> 00:16:22,125
- Did Pat have any money saved?

421
00:16:22,125 --> 00:16:24,167
  - [Crow] Jeez, what is
  he, the Shell Answer Man?

422
00:16:24,167 --> 00:16:25,542
 - Yeah, some.

423
00:16:25,542 --> 00:16:27,250
- Like how much?

424
00:16:27,250 --> 00:16:29,000
 - Well, he was talkin'
 about gettin' a new blower,

425
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:30,042
 and a mill.

426
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:32,625
About 500 bucks.

427
00:16:32,625 --> 00:16:34,125
 - Where did he get
 that kind of money?

428
00:16:34,125 --> 00:16:35,917
 - Bake sale.
 - Saved it.

429
00:16:35,917 --> 00:16:38,000
 His old man gives
 him a good allowance

430
00:16:38,000 --> 00:16:40,042
  when he's not mad at him.

431
00:16:40,042 --> 00:16:41,708
- What bank does he use?

432
00:16:41,708 --> 00:16:46,042
 - [Tom] Hooterville
 Savings and Loan, why?

433
00:16:46,042 --> 00:16:49,000
 - Could've saved it to
 get married, could he?

434
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,333
  - I guess he can do
  whatever he wants with it.

435
00:16:51,333 --> 00:16:54,000
  - [Joel] Looks like the
  garage of Doctor Caligari.

436
00:16:55,250 --> 00:16:57,167
- His old man put him down flat.

437
00:16:57,167 --> 00:16:58,708
  - I know.

438
00:16:58,708 --> 00:17:00,583
 But Pat's smart enough
 to provide for himself

439
00:17:00,583 --> 00:17:02,250
 'til his old man cooled off.

440
00:17:03,417 --> 00:17:06,458
- Dong, dong, dong.
- Sanctuary! Sanctuary!

441
00:17:06,458 --> 00:17:09,083
 - Did you check the hospitals?

442
00:17:09,083 --> 00:17:10,875
- Yeah.

443
00:17:10,875 --> 00:17:13,042
 Where could I find
 the rest of the gang?

444
00:17:13,042 --> 00:17:14,083
 - [Joel] Gang land?

445
00:17:14,083 --> 00:17:15,375
 - I don't know
 about Bob and Gordi,

446
00:17:15,375 --> 00:17:17,167
 but Chuck and Rec
 went over to Easton.

447
00:17:17,167 --> 00:17:19,000
 They wanted to check
 with the Wheel Cats

448
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:20,625
 about next Saturday
 night's platter party.

449
00:17:20,625 --> 00:17:21,792
 - Next Saturday night?

450
00:17:21,792 --> 00:17:23,208
- Yeah.

451
00:17:23,208 --> 00:17:24,708
 - You warn the gang
 I'll be cruising

452
00:17:24,708 --> 00:17:26,042
 that pass that night.

453
00:17:26,042 --> 00:17:27,833
 No draggin'.

454
00:17:27,833 --> 00:17:30,417
 - [Joel] Aw, and he just
 bought those red, satin pumps.

455
00:17:30,417 --> 00:17:33,667
 - You get any postcards
 from those two, let me know.

456
00:17:33,667 --> 00:17:35,917
 - [Crow] Say, nice
 J. Crew barn jacket.

457
00:17:38,042 --> 00:17:39,958
 - [Tom] Meanwhile, at
 Grandma's lake cottage

458
00:17:39,958 --> 00:17:41,292
in Frederic, Wisconsin.

459
00:17:46,875 --> 00:17:47,792
 - Hi Sheriff!

460
00:17:47,792 --> 00:17:49,083
  - [Joel] Hey Mr. Douglas,

461
00:17:49,083 --> 00:17:51,000
 I got those bodies
 buried just in time.

462
00:17:52,125 --> 00:17:54,333
(door knocking)

463
00:17:54,333 --> 00:17:55,583
 - [Tom] Were just
 waiting by the door?

464
00:17:55,583 --> 00:17:56,375
- [Joel] Junior Samples!

465
00:17:56,375 --> 00:17:58,375
- Hello Sheriff.

466
00:17:58,375 --> 00:18:00,083
 (Crow yelling)

467
00:18:00,083 --> 00:18:01,000
 - She's a good girl, Sheriff.

468
00:18:01,000 --> 00:18:02,625
  - [Crow] God, you're ugly.

469
00:18:02,625 --> 00:18:04,042
 - How come you drove around
 the truck all night, then?

470
00:18:04,042 --> 00:18:07,083
 - [Joel] Well, let's just say
 I'm acquainted with the night.

471
00:18:07,083 --> 00:18:08,875
 - You don't think
 she might've eloped?

472
00:18:08,875 --> 00:18:10,125
 - Could be.

473
00:18:10,125 --> 00:18:11,667
  She's pretty closed-mouth
  about her affairs.

474
00:18:11,667 --> 00:18:13,083
- Maude likes a Wheeler.

475
00:18:13,083 --> 00:18:14,458
 He ain't marrying our kind.

476
00:18:14,458 --> 00:18:16,292
  - [Tom] Here's we're just
  simple white trash folk.

477
00:18:16,292 --> 00:18:18,167
 - Just dropped around
 to let you know

478
00:18:18,167 --> 00:18:19,208
 I'm doing everything I can.

479
00:18:19,208 --> 00:18:20,125
- We know that Sheriff.

480
00:18:20,125 --> 00:18:22,000
  We sure do appreciate it.

481
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:24,708
  (spitting)

482
00:18:24,708 --> 00:18:26,917
- Never had any trouble
lookin' after kids.

483
00:18:26,917 --> 00:18:28,708
  - Let me know if I
  can help, Sheriff.

484
00:18:28,708 --> 00:18:30,917
  (blaring)

485
00:18:32,167 --> 00:18:33,667
 - [Man] Quit worryin' this
 way. Got to trust in the Lord.

486
00:18:33,667 --> 00:18:35,167
  - [Crow] Crazy Amish folk.

487
00:18:38,250 --> 00:18:42,708
 (Tom, Joel, and Crow humming
 "The Munsters" theme song)

488
00:18:42,708 --> 00:18:44,458
  - Morning Sheriff.

489
00:18:44,458 --> 00:18:46,000
 - Let me smell your breath.

490
00:18:47,375 --> 00:18:48,208
 - [Crow] Nice uvula.

